  "kimi": {
    "notes": [
      "Deliberately EMPTY. The kimi module's builtin ids are kimi, kimi-k2, k3-agent,",
      "k3-agent-ultra and k2d6-agent. None of them appears in model.json, in",
      "context_catalog.go, in docs/upstream/kimi.md, or in a captured response, so there is",
      "no source for a context window or an output limit. k3-agent is documented as 'K3'",
      "but the id does not match the reference's kimi-k3 entry, and a cross-id inference is",
      "a guess, not a source. Nothing goes in the table until a real response says so."
    ],
    "models": {}
  },
  "tabbit": {
    "notes": [
      "Only ids whose model name matches a reference table id exactly (case-insensitively,",
      "because tabbit lists them capitalised) are filled. The numbers come from the same",
      "public models.dev consensus the reference records for that model; they are NOT",
      "verified against tabbit's own responses, so treat them as a best-effort fallback.",
      "Claude-Opus-4.7, Claude-Sonnet-4.6, Gemini-3.1-Pro, 'priority' (a virtual router",
      "alias) and 'Default' have no sourced entry and stay absent."
    ],
